  },
  "script": "Every codebreaker has one that beats them. Mine is the Voynich manuscript. Two hundred and forty pages, written in a script nobody has ever read. Plants that don't exist. Strange diagrams of the stars. Carbon dating puts the vellum in the early fourteen hundreds. People have claimed to crack it for a century, and every claim has fallen apart. It's sitting in a library at Yale right now. Go on. Have a go."
